uction namespaces are excluded or unmatched, `failurePolicy: Ignore`, or images matching no policy are allowed.\n139\t\n140\t**Reviewer's evidence:** deploy/k8s/kyverno-verify-images.yaml:9 — \"validationFailureAction: Enforce\"\n141\t\n142\t**Reviewer's note:** Policy enforces on procurement-prod with failurePolicy Fail; first rule denies images outside the approved registry\n143\t\n144\t`deploy/k8s/kyverno-verify-images.yaml` lines 1–21 (cited lines marked >):\n145\t```\n146\t   1  apiVersion: kyverno.io/v1\n147\t   2  kind: ClusterPolicy\n148\t   3  metadata:\n149\t   4    name: procurement-verify-images\n150\t   5    annotations:\n151\t   6      policies.kyverno.io/title: Verify procurement agent images\n152\t   7      kyverno.io/kyverno-version: \"1.15.2\"\n153\t   8  spec:\n154\t   9>   validationFailureAction: Enforce\n155\t  10    background: false\n156\t  11    webhookTimeoutSeconds: 15\n157\t  12    failurePolicy: Fail\n158\t  13    rules:\n159\t  14      - name: only-approved-registry\n160\t  15        match:\n161\t  16          any:\n162\t  17            - resources:\n163\t  18                kinds: [Pod]\n164\t  19                namespaces: [procurement-prod]\n165\t  20        validate:\n166\t  21          message: \"Images in procurement-prod must come from registry.example-corp.test/procurement and be pinned by digest.\"\n167\t```\n168\t\n169\t## B10.5\n170\t\n171\t**Check:** The pinned Cosign or verifier version is at least 2.6.2 (2.x) or 3.0.4 (3.x).\n172\t\n173\t**How to verify:** 1) Find Cosign or verifier versions in CI workflows (`cosign-installer`, `cosign-release`), Dockerfiles, and policy-controller charts. 2) Compare to 2.6.2 (2.x) and 3.0.4 (3.x). 3) Answer no if any pin is lower or uses `latest` or no version. Answer unknown if no verifier is in this repo.\n174\t\n175\t**Reviewer's evidence:** .github/workflows/ci.yaml:52 — \"cosign-release: \"v2.6.2\"\"\n176\t\n177\t**Reviewer's note:** Cosign pinned at 2.6.2\n178\t\n179\t`.github/workflows/ci.yaml` lines 40–64 (cited lines marked >):\n180\t```\n181\t  40      if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'\n182\t  41      needs: test\n183\t  42      runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n184\t  43      permissions:\n185\t  44        contents: read\n186\t  45        id-token: write\n187\t  46        packages: write\n188\t  47        attestations: write\n189\t  48      steps:\n190\t  49        - uses: actions/checkout@11bd71901bbe5b1630ceea73d27597364c9af683 # v4.2.2\n191\t  50        - uses: sigstore/cosign-installer@dc72c7d5c4d10cd6bcb8cf6e3fd625a9e5e537da # v3.7.0\n192\t  51          with:\n193\t  52>           cosign-release: \"v2.6.2\"\n194\t  53        - uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@c47758b77c9736f4b2ef4073d4d51994fabfe349 # v3.7.1\n195\t  54        - uses: docker/login-action@9780b0c442fbb1117ed29e0efdff1e18412f7567 # v3.3.0\n196\t  55          with:\n197\t  56            registry: registry.example-corp.test\n198\t  57            username: ${{ github.actor }}\n199\t  58            password: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n200\t  59        - id: build\n201\t  60          uses: docker/build-push-action@4f58ea79222b3b9dc2c8bbdd6debcef730109a75 # v6.9.0\n202\t  61          with:\n203\t  62            context: .\n204\t  63            push: true\n205\t  64            tags: registry.example-corp.test/procurement/agent:${{ github.sha }}\n206\t```\n207\t\n208\t## Your answer\n209\t\n210\tWrite this JSON to B10.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"B10\"):\n211\t```json\n212\t{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n213\t \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"B10.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n214\t \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n215\t```\n216\tVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\n217\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dc26890a-7d29-4465-bb59-9b2c39a47d3d","uuid":"4c4ae4b4-8347-4218-b84c-9c351ca65970","timestamp":"2026-10-02T15:11:35.194Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-6njur4p6/sheet.md","content":"# Challenge: B10 — Pinned, verified image\n\nYou are checking someone else's review. They said every check below is true for this\ncodebase. **Your job is to find a reason one is false.** Read the code shown, and open the\nrepo files if you need more. Assume the reviewer may have misread the code.\n\nFor each check, decide:\n- **holds**: the code shown makes it true in every case you can find;\n- **fails**: you found code that makes it false: a skipped file, a second path, an\n  exception that continues, a value never used, a credential that can undo it, a\n  filter that lets something through. Quote that line;\n- **unclear**: you can't tell from this repo.\n\nThen write your answer for this item in verdicts.json (format at the end).\n\n\n## B10.1\n\n**Check:** Production manifests reference images by digest (`@sha256:`), not by tag alone.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find every `image:` field in manifests, Helm values, compose, and Terraform. 2) Check each uses `@sha256:`. 3) Answer no if any production image uses only a tag (`:latest`, `:v1`), or a template defaults to a tag when the digest value is empty.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:32 — \"image: registry.example-corp.test/procurement/agent@sha256:7c1e4a0f9b3d2e85a6c4f1b0d9e8a7c6b5d4e3f2a1b0c9d8e7f6a5b4c3d2e1f0\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Production image is referenced by digest\n\n`deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml` lines 20–44 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n 